.TH SESSLINT-INIT-HOOKS 1 "" "SessLint 0.2.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-init-hooks \- [read\-only] Print ready\-to\-merge agent hook snippets (never writes config).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint init\-hooks [\-\-agent {claude,codex,all}] [\-\-print] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Print ready\-to\-merge settings.json hook blocks for the documented SessionStart/PreCompact recipes. Print\-only by permanent design — SessLint never writes agent configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex,all}
Agent to generate snippets for (default: all) Choices: claude, codex, all. Default: all.
.TP
.B \-\-print
Print snippets (the only mode — nothing is ever written)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit sesslint.init\-hooks/v1 JSON instead of human text
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

